 "statement": {
  "status": "present",
  "value": "Interactive problem modelled as a deterministic transcript. A simulated game holds target in [0, 999]. query(g) returns \"Correct\" if g = target, \"First\" on the first query otherwise, and afterwards (inferred) \"Hotter\", \"Colder\" or \"Same\" when |g - target| is smaller than, larger than or equal to |previous query - target|. Strategy: keep the set C of targets consistent with every answer so far (initially 0..999; a queried value leaves C unless it was correct). The next query is the only element of C when |C| = 1, otherwise min(C) when an even number of queries has been made and max(C) when odd. Stop at \"Correct\" and return the queried numbers in order.",
  "provenance": [
   {
    "repository": "gamma",
    "revision": null,
    "path": "projects/algorithm_solver/catalogue/authored/hack2hire-chunk06-b-20261028-v1/contracts.json",
    "sha256": "9b45427ee65a0467344aa6db91e9b0ff0426a40d4670db3973ca60de4d6eaf26",
    "selector": "/problems/9/inferred_spec"
   }
  ]
 },
